thon\nclass FakeYDL:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n```\n\nFileDownloader.__init__ might reference ydl.params? Let me check via get_info.\n\nLet me also check DashSegmentsFD and FragmentFD to confirm method names: `_download_fragment`, `_append_fragment`, `_prepare_and_start_frag_download`, `_finish_frag_download`, `report_retry_fragment`, `report_skip_fragment`, `report_error`, and `to_screen`.\n\nLet me make the get_info calls now. I'll batch independent calls:\n\n- 'DashSegmentsFD'\n- 'FragmentFD'\n- 'FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download'\n- 'FragmentFD._download_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._append_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._finish_frag_download'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_skip_fragment'\n- 'FileDownloader.__init__'\n- 'FileDownloader.report_error'\n\nThat's a lot; the tool presumably returns info about symbols in the codebase. Let me do it.\n\nAfter that, write the test file.\n\nLet me draft the test file:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for youtube_dl.downloader.dash.DashSegmentsFD.real_download.\"\"\"\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_urllib_error\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader.dash import DashSegmentsFD\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import DownloadError, urljoin\n\n\nclass FakeYDL(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for YoutubeDL.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n        self.errors = []\n\n\ndef http_error(url):\n    return compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(url, 404, 'Not Found', None, None)\n\n\nclass OutcomeRunner(object):\n    \"\"\"Callable for _download_fragment that replays scripted outcomes per URL.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, script):\n        # script: {url: [outcome, ...]}; outcome is ('ok', bytes) | ('fail', None)\n        # | ('http_error', None) | ('download_error', msg). The last outcome repeats.\n        self.script = dict(script)\n        self.urls = []\n\n    def __call__(self, ctx, url, info_dict):\n        self.urls.append(url)\n        outcomes = self.script.setdefault(url, [('ok', b'fragment-data')])\n        outcome = outcomes.pop(0) if len(outcomes) > 1 else outcomes[0]\n        kind, value = outcome\n        if kind == 'ok':\n            return True, value\n        if kind == 'fail':\n            return False, None\n        if kind == 'http_error':\n            raise http_error(url)\n        if kind == 'download_error':\n            raise DownloadError(value)\n        raise AssertionError('unknown outcome %r' % (kind,))\n\n\ndef make_fd(monkeypatch, params=None, script=None, resume_from=0):\n    \"\"\"Build a DashSegmentsFD with its fragment helpers stubbed out.\"\"\"\n    ydl = FakeYDL()\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(ydl, params or {})\n\n    runner = OutcomeRunner(script or {})\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_download_fragment', runner)\n\n    calls = {'prepare': [], 'append': [], 'finish': [], 'retry': [], 'skip': [], 'error': []}\n\n    def prepare(ctx):\n        calls['prepare'].append(dict(ctx))\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = resume_from\n\n    def append(ctx, content):\n        calls['append'].append(content)\n\n    def finish(ctx):\n        calls['finish'].append(dict(ctx))\n\n    def retry(err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries):\n        calls['retry'].append((frag_index, count, fragment_retries))\n\n    def skip(frag_index):\n        calls['skip'].append(frag_index)\n\n    def error(msg, tb=None, expected=False):\n        calls['error'].append(msg)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_prepare_and_start_frag_download', prepare)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_append_fragment', append)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_finish_frag_download', finish)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_retry_fragment', retry)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_skip_fragment', skip)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_error', error)\n\n    return fd, runner, calls\n\n\ndef frag(url):\n    return {'url': url}\n```\n\nWait \u2014 report_error signature: FileDownloader.report_error(self, msg, tb=None, expected=False)? Let me check with get_info. In youtube_dl/downloader/common.py:\n\n```python\ndef report_error(self, msg, tb=None, expected=False):\n    self.ydl.report_error(msg, tb, expected)\n```\n\nHmm, actually I recall in common.py:\n\n```python\ndef report_error(self, msg, tb=None, expected=False):\n    self.ydl.report_error(msg, tb, expected)\n```\n\nI'll verify with get_info. Similarly report_retry_fragment(self, err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries) and report_skip_fragment(self, frag_index) in fragment.py.\n\nAlso `_prepare_and_start_frag_download(self, ctx)` in fragment.py.\n\nAlso need to double check `DashSegmentsFD.__init__` \u2014 it's FragmentFD's, which is FileDownloader's: `def __init__(self, ydl, params)`. Verify.\n\nAlso `real_download(self, filename, info_dict)`.\n\nNow the tests:\n\n```python\nFRAGMENTS = [\n    {'url': 'http://example.com/seg-1.m4s'},\n    {'url': 'http://example.com/seg-2.m4s'},\n]\n\n\ndef test_success_downloads_all_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    fd, runner, calls = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    info = {'fragments': list(FRAGMENTS)}\n\n    result = fd.real_download('dest.mp4', info)\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert runner.urls == ['http://example.com/seg-1.m4s', 'http://example.com/seg-2.m4s']\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'fragment-data', b'fragment-data']\n    assert len(calls['prepare']) == 1\n    assert len(calls['finish']) == 1\n    assert calls['skip'] == []\n    assert calls['error'] == []\n    assert calls['retry'] == []\n```\n\nCovers: 19, 20-21 (False branch), 23-28, 30-31 defaults, 33-35, 40 (both i==0 fatal and i>0 non-fatal), 42-52, 78, 80.\n\n```python\ndef test_test_mode_downloads_only_first_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    fd, runner, calls = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'test': True})\n    info = {'fragments': list(FRAGMENTS)}\n\n    result = fd.real_download('dest.mp4', info)\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert runner.urls == ['http://example.com/seg-1.m4s']\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'fragment-data']\n    assert 