e.\n- 72: not fatal True/False.\n\nTest list:\n\n1. `test_success_all_fragments`: 2 fragments with 'url', params default. Assert returns True, finish called, appended contents, urls called in order. Covers 19-28, 30-35, 40 (fatal True for i=0, fatal False for i=1), 43-52, 78, 80.\n\n2. `test_test_mode_only_first_fragment`: params {'test': True}, 2 fragments. Assert only 1 download call. Covers 20-21 True branch.\n\n3. `test_resume_skips_downloaded_fragments`: monkeypatch _prepare_and_start_frag_download to set ctx['fragment_index'] = 1. 2 fragments. Assert only second fragment downloaded. Covers 36-37.\n\n4. `test_url_from_path_urljoin`: fragment without 'url', with 'path', fragment_base_url set. Assert downloaded url == urljoin(base, path). Covers 45-47.\n\n5. `test_missing_base_url_asserts`: fragment without 'url', no fragment_base_url. pytest.raises(AssertionError). Covers 46 assert failing.\n\n6. `test_download_fragment_failure_returns_false`: _download_fragment returns (False, None) for first fragment. Assert returns False, finish NOT called. Covers 49-50.\n\n7. `test_http_error_retried_then_success`: first fragment: http_error then ok. params fragment_retries=2. Assert returns True, report_retry_fragment called once with (frag_index=1, count=1, retries=2). Covers 53-62.\n\n8. `test_http_error_gives_up_fatal`: first fragment: http_error always, fragment_retries=1. fatal=True (i==0). Expect report_error called, returns False, finish not called. Covers 61 False branch, 71-76.\n\n9. `test_http_error_gives_up_skip`: second fragment (i=1) http_error always, skip_unavailable_fragments=True (default), fragment_retries=0. Expect report_skip_fragment, returns True, finish called. Covers 71-74.\n\nWait, with fragment_retries=0: while count <= 0: try \u2192 http_error \u2192 count=1; if count <= 0 \u2192 False, no report_retry. Loop: count(1) > 0 \u2192 not fatal \u2192 report_skip_fragment, continue. Good. Covers 61-62 False branch and 71-74.\n\n10. `test_download_error_skipped_nonfatal`: second fragment raises DownloadError, skip default True. Expect report_skip_fragment called, returns True. Covers 63-68.\n\n11. `test_download_error_fatal_first_fragment_raises`: first fragment raises DownloadError. Expect pytest.raises(DownloadError). Covers 69.\n\n12. `test_download_error_fatal_skip_disabled`: second fragment raises DownloadError with skip_unavailable_fragments=False \u2192 fatal=True \u2192 raises. Covers 40 with skip=False and 69.\n\n13. `test_http_error_fatal_skip_disabled`: maybe not needed; 8 covers fatal http give-up.\n\nAlso cover line 30-31 with explicit params: fragment_retries and skip_unavailable_fragments passed in params \u2014 covered by tests 7, 8, 12.\n\nAlso, for line 40 fatal = i == 0 or not skip_unavailable_fragments \u2014 need both operands exercised: i==0 True (tests 8, 11), i>0 & skip True \u2192 False (tests 9, 10), i>0 & skip False \u2192 True (test 12). Good.\n\nNow, about the ctx['fragment_index']: real _prepare_and_start_frag_download sets it. Since we patch it, we set it ourselves. In test 1 etc., set ctx['fragment_index'] = 0.\n\nWait \u2014 actually, should I patch these methods or use the real ones? The real `_prepare_and_start_frag_download` requires a lot of setup (opens file, temp files...). Patching is much cleaner. The instructions say to use monkeypatch where appropriate \u2014 yes.\n\nImplementation detail: monkeypatch.setattr on the instance: `monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_download_fragment', fake)` \u2014 works since monkeypatch.setattr accepts objects with attribute names.\n\nLet me now write the fake ydl. FileDownloader.__init__(self, ydl, params):\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, ydl, params):\n    self._ydl = ydl\n    self.params = params\n    self._progress_hooks = []\n    self._progress_visible = False\n```\n\nHmm, I don't remember exactly. Let me get_info on FileDownloader.__init__ to be sure. Also check whether params needs to be a dict \u2014 yes.\n\nFakeYDL minimal:\n\n```python\nclass FakeYDL:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n```\n\nFileDownloader.__init__ might reference ydl.params? Let me check via get_info.\n\nLet me also check DashSegmentsFD and FragmentFD to confirm method names: `_download_fragment`, `_append_fragment`, `_prepare_and_start_frag_download`, `_finish_frag_download`, `report_retry_fragment`, `report_skip_fragment`, `report_error`, and `to_screen`.\n\nLet me make the get_info calls now. I'll batch independent calls:\n\n- 'DashSegmentsFD'\n- 'FragmentFD'\n- 'FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download'\n- 'FragmentFD._download_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._append_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._finish_frag_download'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_skip_fragment'\n- 'FileDownloader.__init__'\n- 'FileDownloader.report_error'\n\nThat's a lot; the tool presumably returns info about symbols in the codebase. Let me do it.\n\nAfter that, write the test file.\n\nLet me draft the test file:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Tests for youtube_dl.downloader.dash.DashSegmentsFD.real_download.\"\"\"\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_urllib_error\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader.dash import DashSegmentsFD\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import DownloadError, urljoin\n\n\nclass FakeYDL(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for YoutubeDL.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n        self.errors = []\n\n\ndef http_error(url):\n    return compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(url, 404, 'Not Found', None, None)\n\n\nclass OutcomeRunner(object):\n    \"\"\"Callable for _download_fragment that replays scripted outcomes per URL.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, script):\n        # script: {url: [outcome, ...]}; outcome is ('ok', bytes) | ('fail', None)\n        # | ('http_error', None) | ('download_error', msg). The last outcome repeats.\n        self.script = dict(script)\n        self.urls = []\n\n    def __call__(self, ctx, url, info_dict):\n        self.urls.append(url)\n        outcomes = self.script.setdefault(url, [('ok', b'fragment-data')])\n        outcome = outcomes.pop(0) if len(outcomes) > 1 else outcomes[0]\n        kind, value = outcome\n        if kind == 'ok':\n            return True, value\n        if kind == 'fail':\n            return False, None\n        if kind == 'http_error':\n            raise http_error(url)\n        if kind == 'download_error':\n            raise DownloadError(value)\n        raise AssertionError('unknown outcome %r' % (kind,))\n\n\ndef make_fd(monkeypatch, params=None, script=None, resume_from=0):\n    \"\"\"Build a DashSegmentsFD with its fragment helpers stubbed out.\"\"\"\n    ydl = FakeYDL()\n    fd = DashSegmentsFD(ydl, params or {})\n\n    runner = OutcomeRunner(script or {})\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_download_fragment', runner)\n\n    calls = {'prepare': [], 'append': [], 'finish': [], 'retry': [], 'skip': [], 'error': []}\n\n    def prepare(ctx):\n        calls['prepare'].append(dict(ctx))\n        ctx['fragment_index'] = resume_from\n\n    def append(ctx, content):\n        calls['append'].append(content)\n\n    def finish(ctx):\n        calls['finish'].append(dict(ctx))\n\n    def retry(err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries):\n        calls['retry'].append((frag_index, count, fragment_retries))\n\n    def skip(frag_index):\n        calls['skip'].append(frag_index)\n\n    def error(msg, tb=None, expected=False):\n        calls['error'].append(msg)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_prepare_and_start_frag_download', prepare)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_append_fragment', append)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, '_finish_frag_download', finish)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_retry_fragment', retry)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_skip_fragment', skip)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(fd, 'report_error', error)\n\n    return fd, runner, calls\n\n\ndef frag(url):\n    return {'url': url}\n```\n\nWait \u2014 report_error signature: FileDownloader.report_error(self, msg, tb=None, expected=False)? Let me check with get_info. In youtube_dl/downloader/common.py:\n\n```python\ndef report_error(self, msg, tb=None, expected=False):\n    self.ydl.report_error(msg, tb, expected)\n```\n\nHmm, actually I recall in common.py:\n\n```python\ndef report_error(self, msg, tb=None, expected=False):\n    self.ydl.report_error(msg, tb, expected)\n```\n\nI'll verify with get_info. Similarly report_retry_fragment(self, err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries) and report_skip_fragment(self, frag_index) in fragment.py.\n\nAlso `_prepare_and_start_frag_download(self, ctx)` in fragment.py.\n\nAlso need to double check `DashSegmentsFD.__init__` \u2014 it's FragmentFD's, which is FileDownloader's: `def __init__(self, ydl, params)`. Verify.\n\nAlso `real_download(self, filename, info_dict)`.\n\nNow the tests:\n\n```python\nFRAGMENTS = [\n    {'url': 'http://example.com/seg-1.m4s'},\n    {'url': 'http://example.com/seg-2.m4s'},\n]\n\n\ndef test_success_downloads_all_fragments(monkeypatch):\n    fd, runner, calls = make_fd(monkeypatch)\n    info = {'fragments': list(FRAGMENTS)}\n\n    result = fd.real_download('dest.mp4', info)\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert runner.urls == ['http://example.com/seg-1.m4s', 'http://example.com/seg-2.m4s']\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'fragment-data', b'fragment-data']\n    assert len(calls['prepare']) == 1\n    assert len(calls['finish']) == 1\n    assert calls['skip'] == []\n    assert calls['error'] == []\n    assert calls['retry'] == []\n```\n\nCovers: 19, 20-21 (False branch), 23-28, 30-31 defaults, 33-35, 40 (both i==0 fatal and i>0 non-fatal), 42-52, 78, 80.\n\n```python\ndef test_test_mode_downloads_only_first_fragment(monkeypatch):\n    fd, runner, calls = make_fd(monkeypatch, params={'test': True})\n    info = {'fragments': list(FRAGMENTS)}\n\n    result = fd.real_download('dest.mp4', info)\n\n    assert result is True\n    assert runner.urls == ['http://example.com/seg-1.m4s']\n    assert calls['append'] == [b'fragment-data']\n    assert len(call