\n\nAlso need to cover line 40's branches: fatal = i == 0 or not skip_unavailable_fragments. With skip_unavailable_fragments=False, fatal is True even for i>0. Test: DownloadError on second fragment with skip_unavailable_fragments=False \u2192 raise.\n\nLet me check how ctx['fragment_index'] is set. In FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download, ctx gets 'fragment_index' set based on resume. Let me get info.\n\nLet me call get_info for the relevant symbols.\n\nActually, the get_info tool takes a name like 'C.foo'. Let me query:\n- 'DashSegmentsFD'\n- 'FragmentFD'\n- 'FragmentFD._prepare_and_start_frag_download'\n- 'FragmentFD._download_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._append_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD._finish_frag_download'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_retry_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_skip_fragment'\n- 'FragmentFD.report_error'\n- 'FragmentFD._prepare_url'\n\nLet me make these calls in parallel.\n\nThen write the test file.\n\nThe test file structure:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.downloader.dash import DashSegmentsFD\nfrom youtube_dl.compat import compat_urllib_error\nfrom youtube_dl.utils import DownloadError\n\n\nclass FakeDashFD(DashSegmentsFD):\n    \"\"\"Test double that records calls and simulates configurable behavior.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, params=None, download_results=None, http_errors=0, download_errors=0):\n        ...\n```\n\nHmm, DashSegmentsFD.__init__ \u2014 FragmentFD inherits from FileDownloader. FileDownloader.__init__(ydl, params). Let me check. FileDownloader takes (ydl, params). So we can instantiate with a fake ydl.\n\nActually simpler: instantiate DashSegmentsFD with a fake ydl object and params dict, then monkeypatch the fragment methods on the instance.\n\nLet me check FileDownloader.__init__ signature via get_info.\n\nLet me plan the fake ydl: needs to have... FileDownloader.__init__ sets self.ydl = ydl, self.params = params, self._progress_hooks = [], etc. It may call to_screen etc. only when reporting. report_error calls