dex'] = resume_index (default 0).\n- `_download_fragment(ctx, url, info_dict)`: record url; behavior based on configured script; return (True, b'data') or (False, None) or raise HTTPError/DownloadError.\n- `_append_fragment(ctx, content)`: record content.\n- `_finish_frag_download(ctx)`: record call.\n- `report_retry_fragment(err, frag_index, count, fragment_retries)`: record.\n- `report_skip_fragment(frag_index)`: record.\n- `report_error(msg)`: record.\n\nFor HTTPError: compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(url, code, msg, hdrs, fp). Construct with compat_urllib_request or just compat_urllib_error.HTTPError('http://x', 404, 'not found', None, None). That works.\n\nFor DownloadError: DownloadError('msg') \u2014 it's from youtube_dl.utils, subclass of YoutubeDLError. Its __init__ takes msg.\n\nNow the download behavior script: a function or a list of callables. Let me design a flexible fake:\n\n```python\nclass FragmentDownloader:\n    def __init__(self, behavior):\n        self.behavior = behavior  # dict: url fragment index -> list of outcomes\n        self.calls = []\n    def __call__(self, ctx, url, info_dict):\n        self.calls.append(url)\n        outcomes = self.behavior.get(url, [(True, b'data')])\n        outcome = outcomes.pop(0) if len(outcomes) > 1 else outcomes[0]\n        ...\n```\n\nSimpler: use a queue per URL.\n\n```python\ndef _download_fragment(self, ctx, url, info_dict):\n    outcomes = self._outcomes[url]\n    if len(outcomes) > 1:\n        outcome = outcomes.pop(0)\n    else:\n        outcome = outcomes[0]\n    kind, value = outcome\n    if kind == 'ok':\n        return True, value\n    if kind == 'fail':\n        return False, None\n    if kind == 'http_error':\n        raise compat_urllib_error.HTTPError(url, 404, 'Not Found', None, None)\n    if kind == 'download_error':\n        raise DownloadError(value)\n```\n\nNow let me enumerate tests to cover all lines/branches:\n\nLines:\n- 19: fragment_base_url = info_dict.get('fragment_base_url') \u2014 